.TH TH8_API 3 "July 3, 2026" "TH8" "TH8 Library Functions"
.SH NAME
th8_api \- TH8 interpreter C programming interface
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include "th8.h"
.SH DESCRIPTION
This manual page documents the C programming interface to the TH8
interpreter library.  All functions listed here are declared in
.B th8.h
and are available to applications that link against
.BR libth8 .
.SS "Interpreter Lifecycle"
.TP
.BI "Th8_Interp *Th8_CreateInterp(Th8_Platform *" pPlatform ");"
Create a new interpreter.  The platform table is copied internally;
the caller may free or reuse
.I pPlatform
after this call.  Returns NULL on allocation failure.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_DeleteInterp(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Destroy the interpreter and free all resources.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_RestoreInterp(Th8_Interp *" interp ", int " flags ");"
Re-create built-in state after destructive operations (e.g.\&
.BR "namespace delete ::" ).
.I flags
is a bitmask:
.BR TH8_RESTORE_COMMANDS " (0x01),"
.BR TH8_RESTORE_VARIABLES " (0x02),"
.BR TH8_RESTORE_ALL " (0x03)."
.SS "Platform Composability"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_MergePlatform(Th8_Platform *" pDst ", const Th8_Platform *" pSrc ");"
For each NULL callback slot in
.IR pDst ,
copy the value from
.IR pSrc .
If the
.B nVersion
fields of
.I pDst
and
.I pSrc
differ, the merge is skipped and
.B TH8_ERROR
is returned to prevent struct layout mismatches.
Returns
.B TH8_OK
on success.  The
.B pCtx
field is never merged.  Typical usage:
.RS
.nf
.ft CW
Th8_Platform plat = *Th8_GetPosixPlatform();
Th8_MergePlatform(&plat, Th8_GetLibcPlatform());
interp = Th8_CreateInterp(&plat);
.ft
.fi
.RE
.TP
.BI "Th8_Platform *Th8_GetPosixPlatform(void);"
Returns the POSIX platform (I/O, time, stack bounds).
Memory and CRT callbacks are NULL (provided by libc platform).
.TP
.BI "Th8_Platform *Th8_GetWin32Platform(void);"
Returns the Win32 platform.
.TP
.BI "Th8_Platform *Th8_GetNullIoPlatform(void);"
Returns the null I/O platform.  All I/O callbacks are implemented
but produce no side effects: data retrieval returns empty,
output is discarded, binary loading is forbidden,
.B "file exists"
returns 0, and
.B "file normalize"
returns the path verbatim.  Merge with
.B Th8_GetLibcPlatform
for a fully sandboxed interpreter.
.TP
.BI "Th8_Platform *Th8_GetLibcPlatform(void);"
Returns the C runtime platform (memory, memcpy, math, string,
qsort, vsnprintf).
.SS "Script Evaluation"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_Eval(Th8_Interp *" interp ", int " iFrame ", const char *" zProg ", size_t " nProg ", const char *" zName ", size_t " nName ");"
Evaluate script
.I zProg
.RI ( nProg
bytes, or
.B TH8_NOLEN
for NUL-terminated).
.I iFrame
controls scope: 0\ =\ current, negative\ =\ relative
caller, positive\ =\ absolute level.
.I zName / nName
is the script origin name (e.g., the file name from which the
script was loaded); pass NULL/0 if unknown.  The origin name is
forwarded to the pre-eval callback (see
.BR Th8_SetPreEvalCallback ),
enabling policy decisions based on the source of the script.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_EvalDownlevel(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zProg ", size_t " nProg ", const char *" zName ", size_t " nName ");"
Evaluate a script in the caller's frame (equivalent to
.B Th8_Eval
with iFrame=\-1).  This is the implementation of
.BR "[uplevel 1 ...]" .
.I zName / nName
is the script origin name (NULL/0 if unknown), forwarded to the
pre-eval callback.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_Expr(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zExpr ", size_t " nExpr ", const char *" zName ", size_t " nName ");"
Evaluate an expression.  Result is set on the interpreter.
.I zName / nName
is the script origin name (NULL/0 if unknown), forwarded to the
pre-eval callback.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_Complete(const char *" zScript ", size_t " nScript ");"
Returns 1 if braces, brackets, and quotes are balanced
(the script can be evaluated).  Returns 0 if more input is
needed.  Does not require an interpreter.
.SS "NRE (Non-Recursive Engine)"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_NREval(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zProg ", size_t " nProg ", const char *" zName ", size_t " nName ");"
Non-recursive eval: pushes the script onto the NRE callback
chain.  Used by NRE-converted commands instead of
.BR Th8_Eval .
.I zName / nName
is the script origin name (NULL/0 if unknown), forwarded to the
pre-eval callback.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_NRAddCallback(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_CallbackProc " xProc ", void *" p0 ", void *" p1 ", void *" p2 ", void *" p3 ");"
Push a continuation callback.  Callbacks are LIFO: push the
continuation first, then call
.BR Th8_NREval .
.TP
.BI "int Th8_NRInFrame(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_CallbackProc " xCall ", void *" p0 ", void *" p1 ", void *" p2 ", void *" p3 ");"
Push a new call frame with automatic cleanup.  The work callback
.I xCall
runs first; then the frame is popped and freed.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_EvalTrampoline(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Drain all pending NRE callbacks.
.SS "Variables"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetVar(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zVar ", size_t " nVar ");"
Read a variable.  On success, the interpreter result is the value.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_SetVar(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zVar ", size_t " nVar ", const char *" zVal ", size_t " nVal ");"
Set a variable, creating it if necessary.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_UnsetVar(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zVar ", size_t " nVar ");"
Remove a variable.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_ExistsVar(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zVar ", size_t " nVar ");"
Returns 1 if the variable exists, 0 otherwise.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_LinkVar(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zLocal ", size_t " nLocal ", int " iFrame ", const char *" zRemote ", size_t " nRemote ");"
Link a local variable to a variable in another frame.
Used by
.B upvar
and
.BR global .
.SS "Commands"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_CreateCommand(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zName ", Th8_CommandProc " xProc ", void *" pContext ", void (*" xDel ")(Th8_Interp*, void*));"
Register a new command.  If a command with the same name exists,
it is replaced (and its
.I xDel
is called).
.TP
.BI "int Th8_RenameCommand(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zOld ", size_t " nOld ", const char *" zNew ", size_t " nNew ");"
Rename or delete a command.  If
.I zNew
is empty, the command is deleted.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_SetCommandCopy(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zName ", void *(*" xCopy ")(Th8_Interp*, void*));"
Set a deep-copy callback for safe namespace import.
.SS "Result Management"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_SetResult(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ");"
Set the interpreter result string.
.TP
.BI "const char *Th8_GetResult(Th8_Interp *" interp ", size_t *" pn ");"
Return a pointer to the current result.
.TP
.BI "char *Th8_TakeResult(Th8_Interp *" interp ", size_t *" pn ");"
Transfer ownership of the result to the caller.
The caller must free the returned pointer via
.BR Th8_Free .
Refuses for sensitive results: returns NULL and replaces the
interpreter result with an error message.  Sensitive results
must be consumed in place via
.BR Th8_GetResult .
.TP
.BI "int Th8_IsResultSensitive(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return non-zero if the current result is marked sensitive.
Always available; on builds without
.B TH8_ENABLE_CRYPTOGRAPHY
returns 0 because no API is available to set the flag.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_MarkResultSensitive(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Mark the current result as containing sensitive plaintext.
The buffer is securely zeroed via
.B Th8_SecureZero
before being freed on the next overwrite or clear.
Idempotent.  Available only when TH8 is built with
.BR TH8_ENABLE_CRYPTOGRAPHY .
.TP
.BI "int Th8_SetResultSensitive(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ");"
Set the interpreter result to a copy of
.I z
.RI ( n
bytes) stored in a per-interpreter mlock'd, guard-paged
backing region.  The result is automatically marked
sensitive.  Returns
.B TH8_OK
on success or
.B TH8_ERROR
if the value exceeds the region's capacity (one OS page minus
the integrity canary) or if the region cannot be allocated.
The protected region is allocated lazily on first call and
reused for the lifetime of the interpreter.
Available only when TH8 is built with
.BR TH8_ENABLE_CRYPTOGRAPHY .
.TP
.BI "void Th8_SetResultInt(Th8_Interp *" interp ", int " iVal ");"
Set the result to the string representation of
.IR iVal .
.TP
.BI "void Th8_SetResultWideInt(Th8_Interp *" interp ", th8_int64_t " wVal ");"
Set the result to the string representation of a 64-bit integer.
.SS "String and List Operations"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_StringAppend(Th8_Interp *" interp ", char **" pz ", size_t *" pn ", const char *" zApp ", size_t " nApp ");"
Append
.I nApp
bytes to the buffer at
.IR *pz .
The buffer is grown as needed.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_SplitList(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zList ", size_t " nList ", char ***" paz ", size_t **" pan ", int *" pn ");"
Parse a Tcl list into element arrays.  On success \fI*paz\fR, \fI*pan\fR
and the element bytes are ONE allocation; free it with a single
.BI Th8_Free( *paz )
and do not free \fI*pan\fR or the individual elements separately (they
are interior pointers).  \fI*paz\fR/\fI*pan\fR are NULL for zero elements.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_ListAppend(Th8_Interp *" interp ", char **" pz ", size_t *" pn ", const char *" zElem ", size_t " nElem ");"
Append a properly quoted element to a list string.
.SS "Type Conversion"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_ToInt(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ", int *" piVal ");"
Parse a string as a 32-bit integer.  Supports decimal,
.B 0x
hex,
.B 0o
octal,
.B 0b
binary, and leading-zero implicit octal (e.g., 010 = 8).
.TP
.BI "int Th8_ToWideInt(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ", th8_int64_t *" pwVal ");"
Parse a string as a 64-bit integer.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_ToDouble(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ", double *" pdVal ");"
Parse a string as a double-precision float.  Correctly
rounded to nearest-even per IEEE 754 across the entire
finite double range when
.B TH8_ENABLE_BIGINT
is defined (which the default build sets); otherwise
accurate to within 1 ULP on the small minority of
halfway-rounding inputs.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_ToBoolean(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ", int *" pbVal ");"
Parse a string as a boolean (0 or 1).  Accepts integers
(0 = false, nonzero = true) and the case-insensitive strings
.BR true / false ", " yes / no ", " on / off .
.SS "Cancellation"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_CancelEval(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zMsg ", size_t " nMsg ", int " flags ");"
Request asynchronous script cancellation.
.I flags
may include
.B TH8_CANCEL_UNWIND
(prevent
.B catch
from intercepting) and
.B TH8_CANCEL_STATIC
(message is a static string; safe for signal handlers).
.TP
.BI "int Th8_IsCanceled(Th8_Interp *" interp ", int " flags ");"
Check for pending cancellation.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_IsBeingUnwound(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Returns non-zero if cancellation with
.B TH8_CANCEL_UNWIND
is active.
.SS "Cancel-Unwind Recovery"
When
.B TH8_CANCEL_UNWIND
fires during evaluation, the NRE trampoline discards all pending
callbacks (including internal cleanup callbacks) without running
them.  This would leave the eval nesting depth
.RB ( nEvalDepth )
elevated and internal evaluation state leaked.
.PP
To handle this, the outermost
.B Th8_Eval
saves the nesting depth on entry and, when it detects that
cancellation is still active on return, restores
.B nEvalDepth
to the saved value.  If this is the outermost call
(saved depth was 0), the cancellation state is also cleared
automatically so that the interpreter can accept new scripts
without requiring an explicit call to
.BR Th8_ResetCancel .
This enables interactive REPLs and embedding hosts to recover
gracefully after a cancel-unwind event.
.SS "Security Limits"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_Ready(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Unified safety gate.  Checks (in order): native stack overflow,
cancellation, step counter.  Called at every work-unit boundary.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_SetStepLimit(Th8_Interp *" interp ", th8_int64_t " nLimit ");"
Set the maximum number of evaluation steps (0\ =\ unlimited).
.TP
.BI "th8_int64_t Th8_GetStepCount(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Returns the current step count.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_SetResultLimit(Th8_Interp *" interp ", size_t " nLimit ");"
Set the maximum result/string size (0\ =\ use
.BR TH8_MX_STRLEN ).
.TP
.BI "void Th8_SetAllocLimit(Th8_Interp *" interp ", size_t " nLimit ");"
Set the per-interpreter memory ceiling (0\ =\ unlimited).
.TP
.BI "size_t Th8_GetAllocBytes(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Returns total bytes allocated by this interpreter.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_SetOverflowCheck(Th8_Interp *" interp ", int " bEnable ");"
Enable (1) or disable (0) integer overflow detection.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_EnableLoad(Th8_Interp *" interp ", int " bEnable ");"
Enable or disable the
.B xLoad
binary loading callback.  When enabling, a fresh 64-bit random
token is generated from
.BR xRandomBytes .
Returns
.B TH8_ERROR
if no entropy source is available.
The token and gate fields are stored in distant regions of the
interpreter struct to resist linear buffer overflow.
Only the C embedder can call this; scripts cannot enable loading.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_IsLoadEnabled(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Returns non-zero if binary loading is currently enabled.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_EnableUnload(Th8_Interp *" interp ", int " flags ");"
Enable or disable the
.B [unload]
command.  The
.I flags
argument is a bitmask of:
.RS
.TP
.B TH8_UNLOAD_OK
Enable the [unload] command itself.
.TP
.B TH8_UNLOAD_DANGEROUS
Enable actual library closing (dlclose/FreeLibrary) via the
.B \-nokeeplibrary
option.
.RE
.IP
Passing 0 disables unloading entirely.
Each non-zero call regenerates the security token.
Returns
.B TH8_ERROR
if no entropy source is available.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_IsUnloadEnabled(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Returns non-zero if the [unload] command is enabled.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_IsUnloadDangerous(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Returns non-zero if
.B \-nokeeplibrary
(actual library closing) is enabled.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_SetPreLoadCallback(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_PreLoadProc " xProc ", void *" pCtx ");"
Register a callback that is invoked before each
.B [load]
operation.  The callback receives the library name and can veto
the load by returning
.BR TH8_ERROR .
This provides fine-grained per-library access control,
complementing the binary
.B Th8_EnableLoad
gate.  Pass
.I xProc
== NULL to remove the callback.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_Load(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zName ", size_t " nName ", const char *" zProc ", size_t " nProc ");"
Load a binary extension.  Checks the load gate, consults the
pre-load callback (if registered), calls
.BR xLoad ,
and records the library in the tracking list.
Returns
.B TH8_OK
on success.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_Unload(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zName ", size_t " nName ", const char *" zProc ", size_t " nProc ", int " bClose ");"
Unload a previously loaded binary.  Checks the unload gate,
calls
.BR xUnload ,
and removes the library from tracking.
.I bClose
is 0 for
.B \-keeplibrary
(default) or 1 for
.BR \-nokeeplibrary .
.TP
.BI "void *Th8_GetStubs(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the interpreter's stubs table pointer (opaque
.BR "void *" ).
Used internally by
.BR Th8_InitStubs .
.TP
.BI "const Th8StubsTable *Th8_InitStubs(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" version ", int " exact ");"
Initialize the stubs table for a binary extension.
.I version
is the minimum required version string.  If
.I exact
is non-zero, an exact version match is required.
Returns the stubs table pointer on success, or NULL on
version mismatch or failure.
Extensions call this first in their _Init function.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_DataExists(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zName ", size_t " nName ", int *" pAttrs ");"
Test whether named data exists via the platform's
.B xDataExists
callback.  Returns 1 if the data exists, 0 otherwise.
If
.I pAttrs
is non-NULL, the file type attributes are stored there using
.BR TH8_FILE_ATTR_FILE " (1),"
.BR TH8_FILE_ATTR_DIRECTORY " (2),"
.BR TH8_FILE_ATTR_UNSUPPORTED " (3), and"
.BR TH8_FILE_ATTR_SYMLINK " (4, OR'd with FILE or DIRECTORY)."
Pass NULL for
.I pAttrs
if file type information is not needed.
.TP
.BI "char *Th8_NormalizePath(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zPath ", size_t " nPath ");"
Normalize a file path via the platform's
.B xNormalizePath
callback.  Returns a NUL-terminated string allocated via
.BR Th8_Malloc ;
the caller must free it with
.BR Th8_Free .
Returns NULL if the platform callback is not available.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_SetCwd(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zDir ", size_t " nDir ");"
Change the current working directory via the platform's
.B xSetCwd
callback.  The path must resolve to a location at or underneath
the base directory; paths outside the base directory are rejected
with a \(lqpermission denied\(rq error.
Returns
.B TH8_OK
on success,
.B TH8_ERROR
if the callback is not available or the path is rejected.
.TP
\fBTh8_GetCwd\fR(\fIinterp\fR)
Returns the current working directory as a malloc'd UTF-8 string
via the platform's \fBxGetCwd\fR callback.  The caller must free
the result with \fBTh8_Free\fR.  Returns NULL if the callback is
not available or if the current directory is outside the base
directory.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_AutoPathSearch(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Walk the
.B ::auto_path
variable and source every
.B pkgIndex.th8
file found.  For each directory in the list, the variable
.B ::dir
is set to the directory path and the index file is evaluated.
This populates the package hash with
.B "package ifneeded"
entries.  Must be called after language commands are registered.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_MathOp(Th8_Interp *" interp ", int " op ", double *" pResult ", double " a ", double " b ");"
Invoke a platform math function identified by a
.B TH8_MATH_*
operation code.
.I pResult
receives the computed value from arguments
.I a
and
.IR b .
Returns
.B TH8_OK
on success or
.B TH8_ERROR
on failure (e.g.\& unsupported operation).
.SS "Process Lifecycle"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_Initialize(Th8_Platform *" pPlatform ");"
Initialize the TH8 library for use in the current process.
Must be called exactly once before any other TH8 API call.
The
.I pPlatform
provides mutex callbacks for protecting process-global state.
If NULL or mutex callbacks are NULL, TH8 operates in single-threaded
mode.
.RS
.PP
If the platform provides an
.B xInitialize
callback, it is called first, before any other platform callbacks
are used.  This allows the platform to set up internal resources
such as mutexes and heaps.
.PP
After platform initialization,
.B Th8_Initialize
sets the current working directory to the base directory by calling
.BR "xSetCwd(\(dq.\(dq, 1, ...)" .
This establishes \(lq.\(rq as the canonical base path for all
subsequent file system operations.  If
.B xSetCwd
is NULL, the current-directory reset is silently skipped.
.RE
.IP
Returns
.B TH8_OK
on success,
.B TH8_ERROR
on failure.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_Finalize(Th8_Platform *" pPlatform ");"
Finalize the TH8 library, releasing process-global resources.
After this call, no TH8 API may be used until
.B Th8_Initialize
is called again.
If the platform provides an
.B xFinalize
callback, it is called after all other cleanup is complete,
allowing the platform to release internal resources such as
mutexes and heaps.
Returns
.B TH8_OK
on success.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_GlobalMutexEnter(void);"
Enter the process-global mutex.  No-op in single-threaded mode.
Used by platform code to protect process-global state.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_GlobalMutexLeave(void);"
Leave the process-global mutex.
.TP
\fBTh8_MemBarrier\fR()
Issues a full memory barrier via the platform's \fBxMemBarrier\fR
callback, ensuring all prior writes are visible to other threads.
No-op if the callback is NULL (single-threaded mode).
.TP
\fBTh8_EmitTrace\fR(\fIzFmt\fR, ...)
Emit a formatted diagnostic trace message via the platform's
\fBxEmitTrace\fR callback.  Accepts \fBprintf\fR\-style format
and arguments.  The formatted message is truncated to 512 bytes.
No-op if the callback is NULL.  Available in all builds; the
\fBTH8_TRACE_ERR\fR macro (debug builds only) calls this with
the source file, line number, a message, and the system error
code (\fBerrno\fR on POSIX, \fBGetLastError()\fR on Win32).
.SS "Frames and Introspection"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_InFrame(Th8_Interp *" interp ", int (*" xCall ")(Th8_Interp*, void*, void*), void *" p1 ", void *" p2 ");"
Push a new frame, call
.IR xCall ,
pop the frame.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_SetFrameObjv(Th8_Interp *" interp ", int " argc ", const char **" argv ", size_t *" argl ");"
Store invocation info on the current frame for
.BR "info level" .
Pointers are borrowed; must outlive the frame.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetFrameLevel(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Returns the current procedure nesting level (0\ =\ global).
.SS "Parsing"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_ParseCommand(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zScript ", size_t " nScript ", int " iLine ", Th8_Parse *" pParse ");"
Parse the first command in
.IR zScript .
.I nScript
is the byte length (or
.B TH8_NOLEN
for NUL-terminated).
.I iLine
is the starting line number (for error reporting).
On success, the
.I pParse
structure is populated with token information.
Returns
.B TH8_OK
or
.BR TH8_ERROR .
The caller must call
.B Th8_FreeParse
when finished with the parse result.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_ParseVarName(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zStr ", size_t " nStr ", Th8_Value *" pValue ");"
Parse a variable reference starting with
.BR $ .
.I zStr
points to the
.B $
character;
.I nStr
is the length of the remaining string.
On success,
.I pValue
is populated with the parsed variable name.
Returns
.B TH8_OK
or
.BR TH8_ERROR .
.TP
.BI "int Th8_ParseExpr(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zExpr ", size_t " nExpr ", Th8_Parse *" pParse ");"
Parse an expression string into tokens without evaluating it.
.I nExpr
is the byte length (or
.B TH8_NOLEN
for NUL-terminated).
On success, the
.I pParse
structure is populated with the expression's token tree.
Returns
.B TH8_OK
or
.BR TH8_ERROR .
The caller must call
.B Th8_FreeParse
when finished with the parse result.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_FreeParse(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_Parse *" pParse ");"
Free the token arrays in a
.B Th8_Parse
structure previously filled by
.B Th8_ParseCommand
or
.BR Th8_ParseExpr .
Does not free the
.B Th8_Parse
struct itself; only its internal allocations are released.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_ByteToUtf16Col(const char *" zLine ", size_t " nLine ", size_t " iByte ");"
Convert a UTF-8 byte offset to a UTF-16 column index.
.I zLine
is the line text,
.I nLine
is the line length in bytes, and
.I iByte
is the zero-based byte offset within the line.
Returns the zero-based UTF-16 column index.
Uses
.B ConvertUTF_v2
for the conversion.
.SS "Namespaces"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_FindNamespace(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zName ", size_t " nName ", int " bCreate ");"
Check/create a namespace.  Returns 1 if found (or created).
.TP
.BI "int Th8_DeleteNamespace(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zName ", size_t " nName ");"
Delete a namespace and all its contents.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_NsEval(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zNs ", size_t " nNs ", const char *" zScript ", size_t " nScript ");"
Evaluate \fIzScript\fR in the context of the namespace named
by \fIzNs\fR (creating it if it does not exist).  A new call
frame is pushed for the duration so that \fBuplevel\fR can
correctly identify the namespace context.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_NsExport(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zNs ", size_t " nNs ", const char *" zPattern ", size_t " nPattern ");"
Add export patterns to a namespace.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_NsImport(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zPattern ", size_t " nPattern ", int " bForce ");"
Import exported commands matching \fIzPattern\fR (a fully
qualified glob, e.g., \fB::foo::*\fR) into the current
namespace.  Imported commands are deep-copied if the source
command has a copy callback (see \fBTh8_SetCommandCopy\fR);
otherwise the context pointer is shared.  Imported commands
retain the defining namespace of the source command, so
\fBnamespace current\fR and the \fBvariable\fR command within
an imported proc operate on the original namespace.
.RS
.PP
If \fIbForce\fR is non-zero, existing commands in the target
namespace are silently overwritten.  If \fIbForce\fR is zero,
commands that already exist in the target namespace are
skipped.
.RE
.TP
.BI "void *Th8_GetCurrentNsPtr(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return an opaque pointer to the interpreter's current namespace.
This is used by extension code that needs to save and later
restore the namespace context (e.g., when dispatching a proc
defined in a different namespace).
.TP
.BI "void Th8_SetCurrentNsPtr(Th8_Interp *" interp ", void *" pNs ");"
Set the interpreter's current namespace to \fIpNs\fR, which
must be a pointer previously obtained from
.BR Th8_GetCurrentNsPtr .
.TP
.BI "void Th8_SetFrameNsPtr(Th8_Interp *" interp ", void *" pNs ");"
Set the namespace recorded in the current call frame to
\fIpNs\fR.  This is used in conjunction with
.B Th8_SetCurrentNsPtr
to ensure that \fBuplevel\fR correctly identifies the
namespace context of the frame.
.SS "Memory"
.TP
.BI "void *Th8_Malloc(Th8_Interp *" interp ", size_t " nByte ");"
Allocate zero-filled memory via the platform.
Calls
.B xPanic
on failure.
.TP
.BI "void *Th8_Realloc(Th8_Interp *" interp ", void *" p ", size_t " nByte ");"
Resize a block.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_Free(Th8_Interp *" interp ", void *" p ");"
Free a block allocated by
.B Th8_Malloc
or
.BR Th8_Realloc .
.SS "Hash Table"
.TP
.BI "Th8_Hash *Th8_HashNew(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Create a new hash table.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_HashDelete(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_Hash *" pHash ");"
Delete an entire hash table and all its entries.
.TP
.BI "Th8_HashEntry *Th8_HashFind(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_Hash *" pHash ", const char *" zKey ", size_t " nKey ", int " op ");"
Find, create, or delete a hash entry.
.I op
< 0 deletes, 0 finds, > 0 creates.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_HashRemove(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_Hash *" pHash ", const char *" zKey ", size_t " nKey ");"
Remove a single entry by key.  Does NOT free
.BR pData .
.TP
.BI "void Th8_HashIterate(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_Hash *" pHash ", int (*" xCallback ")(Th8_HashEntry*, void*), void *" pCtx ");"
Call
.I xCallback
for each entry.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_HashIterateOrdered(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_Hash *" pHash ", Th8_HashIterProc " xProc ", void *" pCtx ");"
Iterate hash entries in insertion order
(complementing
.BR Th8_HashIterate ,
which visits entries in undefined/hash-bucket order).
.SS "Language Registration"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_RegisterLanguage(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Register all built-in commands.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_RegisterRegex(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Register
.B regexp
and
.B regsub
commands.  Only available when compiled with
.BR TH8_ENABLE_REGEXP .
.SS "Exit Flag"
.TP
.BI "void Th8_Exit(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Set the interpreter's exit flag.  Once set,
.B Th8_Ready
returns
.B TH8_ERROR
on every call, unwinding the entire call stack.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_IsExited(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return non-zero if the exit flag is set.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_ResetExit(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Clear the exit flag so the interpreter can resume execution.
This is the only way to clear the exit state.
.SS "Suspension (Freeze / Thaw)"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_Freeze(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Suspend the interpreter.  The current NRE callback chain is detached
and saved so that evaluation can be resumed later via
.BR Th8_Thaw .
Returns
.BR TH8_SUSPEND .
.TP
.BI "int Th8_Thaw(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Resume a previously frozen interpreter by draining the saved
callback chain.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_IsSuspended(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return non-zero if the interpreter is currently suspended.
.SS "File Evaluation"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_EvalFile(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zPath ", size_t " nPath ");"
Read the named file via the platform
.B xGetData
callback and evaluate its contents.  Equivalent to the script-level
.B source
command.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_EvalFileAsData(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zName ", size_t " nName ", const unsigned char **" pzData ", size_t *" pnData ", void *" pCtx ");"
Load binary data by evaluating a signed script in an isolated child
interpreter.  Creates a temporary child that inherits the parent's
platform callbacks and signed\-only policy (if active).  The named file
is evaluated in the child via
.BR Th8_EvalFile ;
on success the child's result is base64\-decoded and returned via
.I pzData
and
.IR pnData .
The child is always deleted.  The caller must free
.I *pzData
with
.BR Th8_Free .
.I pCtx
is reserved and must be NULL.
Primary use case: loading additional RSA public keys (as base64\-encoded
SNK blobs) into the signed\-script policy context, where the
key\-delivery script itself must pass signature verification.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_EvalFileAndRsaKeyLoad(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zName ", size_t " nName ", void *" pCtx ", int " bPreload ");"
Convenience function that combines
.B Th8_EvalFileAsData
(evaluate a signed script in a child interpreter and base64\-decode the
result) with
.B Th8_RsaKeyLoad
(parse the decoded data as an SNK/CAPI RSA key).
If
.I bPreload
is non\-zero, the key is preloaded into the signed\-only policy cache
via
.BR Th8_PolicyPreloadKey ;
.I pCtx
must be the opaque policy context in that case.
Returns
.B TH8_OK
on success.
Gated by
.BR TH8_ENABLE_CRYPTOGRAPHY .
.SS "Base Path"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_SetBasePath(const char *" zPath ", int " bNormalize ");"
Set or override the base directory used by the file system security
model.  If
.I bNormalize
is non-zero, the path is resolved via the platform's
.B xNormalizePath
callback.
.SS "UTF-8 Utilities"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_Utf8Decode(const char *" z ", size_t " n ", int *" pnByte ");"
Decode one Unicode code point from the UTF-8 string
.IR z .
Stores the byte count consumed in
.IR *pnByte .
Returns the code point value.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_Utf8Encode(int " codepoint ", char *" z ");"
Encode a single Unicode code point as UTF-8 into
.IR z .
Returns the number of bytes written (1\(en4).
.TP
.BI "int Th8_Utf8Len(const char *" z ", size_t " n ");"
Return the number of Unicode characters in the UTF-8 string.
.TP
.BI "const char *Th8_Utf8Advance(const char *" z ", size_t " n ", int " nChar ");"
Advance
.I nChar
characters into the UTF-8 string.  Returns a pointer to that position.
.TP
.BI "const char *Th8_Utf8Index(const char *" z ", size_t " n ", int " iChar ");"
Return a pointer to character
.I iChar
in the UTF-8 string.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_Utf8Validate(const char *" z ", size_t " n ", int *" piOffset ");"
Validate that
.I z
is well-formed UTF-8.  If invalid, stores the byte offset of the
first bad byte in
.IR *piOffset .
Returns non-zero if valid.
.SS "Character Classification"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_IsDigit(int " c ");"
.TQ
.BI "int Th8_IsSpace(int " c ");"
.TQ
.BI "int Th8_IsAlnum(int " c ");"
.TQ
.BI "int Th8_IsAlpha(int " c ");"
.TQ
.BI "int Th8_IsSpecial(int " c ");"
.TQ
.BI "int Th8_IsHexDig(int " c ");"
.TQ
.BI "int Th8_IsOctDig(int " c ");"
.TQ
.BI "int Th8_IsBinDig(int " c ");"
ASCII character classification functions.  These do not depend on the
C locale and are safe to call from any thread.
.SS "String Utilities"
.TP
.BI "size_t Th8_Strlen(const char *" z ");"
Return the length of a NUL-terminated string.
.TP
.BI "char *Th8_Strdup(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ");"
Allocate a copy of
.I n
bytes of
.I z
via
.BR Th8_Malloc .
The copy is NUL-terminated.
.SS "Platform-Routed Utility Wrappers"
These functions route through the corresponding
.B Th8_Platform
callbacks.  They return sensible defaults (0, NULL, no-op)
when the callback is NULL.
.TP
.BI "void *Th8_Memmove(Th8_Interp *" interp ", void *" dst ", const void *" src ", size_t " n ");"
Move
.I n
bytes from
.I src
to
.I dst
(overlapping regions permitted) via
.BR xMemmove .
Returns
.IR dst .
.TP
.BI "int Th8_Strcmp(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" s1 ", const char *" s2 ");"
Compare two NUL-terminated strings via
.BR xStrcmp .
.TP
.BI "char *Th8_Strchr(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" s ", int " c ");"
Locate the first occurrence of byte
.I c
in string
.I s
via
.BR xStrchr .
.TP
.BI "int Th8_Atoi(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" s ");"
Convert a NUL-terminated decimal string to int via
.BR xAtoi .
.TP
.BI "void Th8_Qsort(Th8_Interp *" interp ", void *" base ", size_t " nmemb ", size_t " size ", int (*" cmp ")(const void *, const void *));"
Sort an array in place via
.BR xQsort .
.TP
.BI "int Th8_Vsnprintf(Th8_Interp *" interp ", char *" buf ", size_t " size ", const char *" fmt ", va_list " ap ");"
Formatted output into a buffer via
.BR xVsnprintf .
.TP
.BI "int Th8_Snprintf(Th8_Interp *" interp ", char *" buf ", size_t " size ", const char *" fmt ", ...);"
Variadic convenience wrapper around
.BR Th8_Vsnprintf .
.SS "Types and Macros"
.TP
\fBTh8_Mutex\fR
Platform-specific mutex type defined in \fBth8_plat.h\fR.
On Windows, this is \fBCRITICAL_SECTION\fR.  On POSIX, this is
\fBpthread_mutex_t\fR.  Used by the \fBxMutexInit\fR,
\fBxMutexFinal\fR, \fBxMutexEnter\fR, and \fBxMutexLeave\fR
platform callbacks.
.TP
\fBTH8_API\fR
Decoration macro for public API functions.  On Windows, expands to
\fB__declspec(dllexport)\fR when building the TH8 DLL
(\fBTH8_BUILD_DLL\fR defined) and to \fB__declspec(dllimport)\fR
when consuming it.  On GCC/Clang, uses
\fB__attribute__((visibility("default")))\fR.
.SS "String Substitution"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_Subst(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ", int " flags ");"
Perform Tcl-style substitutions on the string
.IR z .
The
.I flags
argument is a bitmask of
.BR TH8_SUBST_BACKSLASHES " (1), "
.BR TH8_SUBST_COMMANDS " (2), "
.BR TH8_SUBST_VARIABLES " (4)."
.B TH8_SUBST_ALL
(7) enables all three.
The result is stored in the interpreter result.
Command substitutions that return
.B TH8_BREAK
stop processing;
.B TH8_CONTINUE
replaces the command with the empty string;
.B TH8_RETURN
uses the return value.
.SS "Internal-Representation Cache"
A per-interpreter hash table that caches the result of
string-to-value conversions.  Protected by a per-interpreter mutex.
.TP
.BI "Th8_Value *Th8_FindInCache(Th8_Interp *" interp ", int " cacheType ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ");"
Look up or create a cache entry keyed by
.RI ( cacheType ", " z ).
Returns a cache-owned
.B Th8_Value
pointer; the caller should check the type-specific union
.B iValid
flag and populate on miss.  Cache types:
.BR TH8_CACHE_INT " (1), "
.BR TH8_CACHE_WIDE " (2), "
.BR TH8_CACHE_DOUBLE " (3), "
.BR TH8_CACHE_BIGINT " (4), "
.BR TH8_CACHE_BOOL " (5), "
.BR TH8_CACHE_STRING " (7), "
.BR TH8_CACHE_LIST " (8), "
.BR TH8_CACHE_COMMAND " (9)."
.TP
.BI "Th8_Value *Th8_FindListInCache(Th8_Interp *" interp ", int " cacheType ", int " nElem ", const char **" azElem ", const size_t *" anElem ");"
List-keyed variant.  Hash is computed from element count XOR'd
with each element hash (order-sensitive).
.TP
.BI "void Th8_ClearCache(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Discard all cache entries and free all associated memory.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_RemoveFromCache(Th8_Interp *" interp ", int " cacheType ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ");"
Remove a single cache entry.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_SetCacheString(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_Value *" pVal ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ");"
Set the string representation on a list-keyed cache entry
(returned by
.BR Th8_FindListInCache )
whose
.B zData
was initially NULL.
.TP
.BI "Th8_Value *Th8_CopyValue(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const Th8_Value *" pSrc ");"
Deep-copy a cache-borrowed
.BR Th8_Value .
The caller owns the result and must free it with
.BR Th8_FreeValue .
.TP
.BI "void Th8_FreeValue(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_Value *" pVal ");"
Free a value returned by
.BR Th8_CopyValue .
.SS "Platform: Executable Path"
.TP
.BI "char *(*xGetExePath)(void *" interp ", void *" pCtx ");"
Platform callback returning the fully qualified path to the
running executable.  The result is allocated via
.BR Th8_Malloc ;
the caller frees it.
Used by
.B "info nameofexecutable"
when the
.B ::th8_nameofexecutable
variable is not set.
Linux uses
.IR /proc/self/exe ;
macOS uses
.IR _NSGetExecutablePath ;
Win32 uses
.IR GetModuleFileNameA .
.SS "Platform Wrapper Functions"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_RandomBytes(Th8_Interp *" interp ", void *" pBuf ", size_t " nByte ");"
Fill
.I pBuf
with
.I nByte
random bytes from the platform's
.B xRandomBytes
entropy source.
Returns
.B TH8_OK
on success, or
.B TH8_ERROR
if the platform does not provide an entropy source.
.TP
.BI "char *Th8_GetExePath(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the fully qualified path to the current executable via the
platform's
.B xGetExePath
callback.  The returned string is allocated via
.BR Th8_Malloc ;
the caller must free it with
.BR Th8_Free .
Returns NULL if the platform does not provide
.BR xGetExePath .
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetParentPid(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the parent process ID via the platform's
.B xGetParentPid
callback.  Returns 0 if the callback is not available.
.TP
.BI "th8_uint64_t Th8_GetThreadId(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the current thread ID as a 64-bit unsigned integer via the
platform's
.B xGetThreadId
callback.  Returns 0 if the callback is not available.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetRootPath(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zPath ", size_t " nPath ", char *" zOut ", size_t " nOut ");"
Resolve the filesystem root or mount point for
.I zPath
via the platform's
.B xGetRootPath
callback.  The result is written to
.IR zOut .
On POSIX, this is typically
.BR / .
On Windows, this is the volume root (e.g.,
.BR C:\e ).
Returns
.B TH8_OK
on success, or
.B TH8_ERROR
if the callback is not available.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_SameFile(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zPath1 ", size_t " nPath1 ", const char *" zPath2 ", size_t " nPath2 ");"
Compare two paths for physical file identity via the platform's
.B xSameFile
callback.  Returns non-zero if both paths refer to the same file
(inode/device on POSIX, file identity on Windows).  Returns 0 if
the files are different or the callback is not available.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_ListAppendVarLinks(Th8_Interp *" interp ", char **" pz ", size_t *" pn ");"
Append the names of all linked variables in the current call frame
to the list at
.IR *pz .
A linked variable is one created by
.BR upvar ", " global ", or " variable .
Returns
.B TH8_OK
on success.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetEvalDepth(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the current script evaluation nesting depth.
0 means no evaluation is active, 1 means the outermost
.B Th8_Eval
call is running, and values greater than 1 indicate nested
evaluation (e.g., from
.B [eval]
or
.B [source]
within a running script).
.TP
.BI "int Th8_TranslateLineEndings(char *" zBuf ", size_t *" pnBuf ");"
Verify that all newline characters in
.I zBuf
are preceded by carriage return (i.e., all line endings are
.BR \er\en ),
then translate each
.B \er\en
pair to a single
.B \en
in-place.
.I *pnBuf
is updated to reflect the new length.
Returns
.B TH8_OK
on success, or
.B TH8_ERROR
if a bare
.B \en
(not preceded by
.BR \er )
is found.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_ResetSecurityArray(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Set all elements of the
.B ::th8_security
array to the string
.BR none .
This is typically called before script signature verification
to ensure a clean baseline.
Returns
.B TH8_OK
on success.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_NotifyDeleteInterp(Th8_Interp *" interp ", void *" pCtx ");"
Invoke the platform's
.B xDeleteInterp
callback, passing
.I interp
and
.IR pCtx .
This notifies the host application that the interpreter is being
destroyed, allowing it to clean up any associated resources.
.SS "Platform Callback: xCloseTemporaryData"
The
.B xCloseTemporaryData
callback is called before explicitly closing a temporary channel.
It receives the channel handle and may return
.B TH8_OK
to allow the close or
.B TH8_ERROR
to veto it (the channel remains open).
If the callback is NULL, the close is always allowed.
This callback sits in
.B Th8_Platform
after
.BR xSetTemporaryData .
.SH "SCRIPT SIGNATURE VERIFICATION"
When compiled with
.BR TH8_ENABLE_CRYPTOGRAPHY ,
TH8 supports a signed-only evaluation mode in which every script
must be accompanied by a valid RSA signature before it is executed.
This provides code provenance and tamper detection for deployments
that require strong script integrity guarantees.
.SS "Enabling signed-only mode"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_EnableSignedOnly(Th8_Interp *" interp ", int " bEnable ");"
Enable or disable the signed-only script evaluation gate.  Uses
the same random-token security pattern as
.BR Th8_EnableLoad .
Returns
.B TH8_ERROR
if no entropy source is available.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_IsSignedOnlyEnabled(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Returns non-zero if signed-only mode is currently enabled.
.SS "Installing and removing the policy"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_InstallSignedPolicy(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Install the signed-only pre-eval callback.  When signed-only mode
is enabled (via
.BR Th8_EnableSignedOnly ),
the callback is invoked before each script evaluation.  For every
script whose origin name is known (i.e., the
.I zName
parameter passed to
.BR Th8_Eval ,
.BR Th8_EvalFile ,
etc.\& is non-NULL), the callback:
.RS
.IP 1. 4
Resets the
.B ::th8_security
array to
.BR none .
.IP 2. 4
Reads the companion signature file
.IB name .b64sig
via the platform's
.B xGetData
callback.  The signature file contains a Harpy-format header
(algorithm, public key token) followed by the base64-encoded RSA
signature.
.IP 3. 4
Resolves the public key by matching the token from the signature
header against the key registry.
.IP 4. 4
Verifies the RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 SHA-512 signature over the script
data using the resolved public key.
.IP 5. 4
On success, populates the
.B ::th8_security
array with the verified details and allows evaluation to proceed.
On failure, returns
.B TH8_ERROR
with a diagnostic message.
.RE
.TP
.BI "void Th8_RemoveSignedPolicy(Th8_Interp *" interp ", void *" pCtx ");"
Remove the signed-only pre-eval callback and free its context.
.I pCtx
is the opaque context pointer obtained from the interpreter's
pre-eval state; pass NULL for a no-op.
.SS "The ::th8_security array"
When a signed script is successfully verified, the following
elements are set:
.TP
.B ::th8_security(algorithmName)
The signature algorithm, e.g.,
.BR RSA-2048 .
Set to
.B none
before verification and on failure.
.TP
.B ::th8_security(policy)
The verification policy status.  Set to
.B signed
on success, or
.B none
before verification and on failure.
.TP
.B ::th8_security(publicKeyToken)
The 16-character hexadecimal public key token that identifies
which key was used to sign the script.  Set to
.B none
before verification and on failure.
.SS "RSA verification"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_RsaVerify(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const Th8_RsaKey *" pKey ", const unsigned char *" zData ", size_t " nData ", const unsigned char *" zSig ", size_t " nSig ");"
Verify an RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 SHA-512 signature.
.I pKey
is the public key,
.I zData / nData
is the data that was signed, and
.I zSig / nSig
is the raw signature bytes.
Returns
.B TH8_OK
if the signature is valid,
.B TH8_ERROR
otherwise.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_RsaExtractHash(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const Th8_RsaKey *" pKey ", const unsigned char *" zSig ", size_t " nSig ", unsigned char *" zOut ");"
Recover the SHA-512 hash from an RSA PKCS#1 v1.5 signature.
.I pKey
is the public key used to decrypt the signature block.
.I zSig / nSig
is the raw signature bytes.  The recovered 64-byte SHA-512 hash
is written to
.IR zOut ,
which must be at least 64 bytes.
Returns
.B TH8_OK
on success, or
.B TH8_ERROR
if the signature padding is invalid or the key cannot decrypt
the block.
.SS "SHA-512"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_Sha512Hex(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const unsigned char *" zData ", size_t " nData ", char *" zOut ");"
Compute the SHA-512 digest of
.I zData
.RI ( nData
bytes) and write the 128-character hexadecimal representation to
.IR zOut ,
which must be at least 129 bytes (128 hex digits plus NUL
terminator).
Returns
.B TH8_OK
on success.
.SS "RSA key management"
.TP
.B "typedef struct Th8_RsaKey Th8_RsaKey;"
Opaque type representing a parsed RSA key (public or private).
.TP
.BI "int Th8_RsaKeyLoad(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const unsigned char *" zData ", size_t " nData ", Th8_RsaKey **" ppKey ");"
Parse a binary key blob (SNK format) into an
.B Th8_RsaKey
structure.  The caller must free with
.BR Th8_RsaKeyFree .
.TP
.BI "void Th8_RsaKeyFree(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_RsaKey *" pKey ");"
Free a key returned by
.BR Th8_RsaKeyLoad .
.TP
.BI "int Th8_RsaKeyBitLen(const Th8_RsaKey *" pKey ");"
Return the key length in bits (e.g., 2048).
.TP
.BI "int Th8_RsaKeyToken(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const Th8_RsaKey *" pKey ", unsigned char " zOut "[8]);"
Compute the 8-byte binary public key token for
.IR pKey .
.TP
.BI "int Th8_RsaKeyTokenHex(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const Th8_RsaKey *" pKey ", char " zOut "[17]);"
Compute the 16-character hexadecimal public key token for
.IR pKey .
The output buffer must be at least 17 bytes (16 hex digits plus
NUL terminator).
.SS "Policy key pre-loading"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_PolicyPreloadKey(Th8_Interp *" interp ", void *" pCtx ", Th8_RsaKey *" pKey ");"
Pre-load an RSA key into the signed-only policy cache so that
signature verification can proceed without fetching the key from
the network.  The policy takes ownership of
.IR pKey ;
the caller must not free it after this call.
.I pCtx
is the opaque context pointer from
.BR Th8_InstallSignedPolicy .
Returns
.B TH8_OK
on success.
.SS "Signed-only gate save/restore"
.TP
.BI "void Th8_SaveSignedOnly(Th8_Interp *" interp ", void *" pSaved ");"
Save the current signed-only gate state into the caller-provided
buffer
.IR pSaved ,
which must be at least
.B TH8_SIGNED_SAVE_SIZE
(16) bytes.  This allows the host to temporarily bypass policy
enforcement (e.g., when reading auxiliary files that are not
themselves signed).
.TP
.BI "void Th8_RestoreSignedOnly(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const void *" pSaved ");"
Restore the signed-only gate state from
.IR pSaved ,
which was previously filled by
.BR Th8_SaveSignedOnly .
.TP
.B "TH8_SIGNED_SAVE_SIZE (16)"
Minimum size in bytes of the buffer passed to
.B Th8_SaveSignedOnly
and
.BR Th8_RestoreSignedOnly .
.SS "Convenience policy setup"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_EnableSignedPolicy(Th8_Interp *" interp ", void **" ppCtx ", int " bEnable ");"
One-call convenience to install or remove the signed-only policy.
When
.I bEnable
is 1: installs the signed-only pre-eval callback via
.BR Th8_InstallSignedPolicy ,
preloads all embedded keys (both
.B keyRoot
and
.BR key0 )
into the policy cache, enables the signed-only gate, and writes
the opaque policy context pointer to
.IR *ppCtx .
When
.I bEnable
is 0: disables the signed-only gate, removes the policy via
.BR Th8_RemoveSignedPolicy ,
and cleans up the context.
Returns
.B TH8_OK
on success, or
.B TH8_ERROR
on failure (e.g., if no entropy source is available or key
loading fails).
.SH "EMBEDDED PUBLIC KEYS"
TH8 supports embedding public keys directly into the compiled
binary so that signature verification can proceed without
external key files.  Keys are generated from binary SNK
(Strong Name Key) files using the
.B tools/mkkey.tcl
utility.
.SS "Key embedding tool"
.TP
.B "tclsh tools/mkkey.tcl" \fIkeyFile.snk\fR
Reads a binary SNK file and produces a C source file at
.BI src/crypto/th8_ baseName .c
containing the key data as a
.B "static const unsigned char"
array with an accessor function.  The generated file is compiled
into the TH8 library and provides the raw key bytes at runtime.
.SS "Accessing embedded keys"
.TP
.BI "const unsigned char *Th8_GetEmbeddedKeyRoot(size_t *" pnData ");"
Returns a pointer to the embedded root key data.  If
.I pnData
is non-NULL, the size in bytes is stored there.  The root key
is the trust anchor for the key hierarchy.
.TP
.BI "const unsigned char *Th8_GetEmbeddedKey0(size_t *" pnData ");"
Returns a pointer to the embedded key0 data (the built-in public
key used for script signature verification).  If
.I pnData
is non-NULL, the size in bytes is stored there.
.TP
.BI "Th8_RsaKey *Th8_GetPublicKeyZero(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Load the embedded key0 as a parsed
.B Th8_RsaKey
structure.  The returned key is cached internally by the policy
context and must NOT be freed by the caller.  Returns NULL on
parse failure.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetPublicKeyZeroToken(Th8_Interp *" interp ", char " zOut "[17]);"
Compute the 16-character hexadecimal public key token for the
embedded key0.  The output buffer must be at least 17 bytes.
Returns
.B TH8_OK
on success.
.TP
.BI "Th8_RsaKey *Th8_GetPublicKeyRoot(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Load the embedded root key as a parsed
.B Th8_RsaKey
structure.  The returned key is cached internally and must NOT be
freed by the caller.  Returns NULL on parse failure.  The root key
is the trust anchor for the key hierarchy.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetPublicKeyRootToken(Th8_Interp *" interp ", char " zOut "[17]);"
Compute the 16-character hexadecimal public key token for the
embedded root key.  The output buffer must be at least 17 bytes
(16 hex digits plus NUL terminator).
Returns
.B TH8_OK
on success.
.SS "Test key APIs"
The following functions are available when compiled with
.BR ENABLE_TEST_KEY=1 .
They provide access to an embedded test key for development and
testing purposes.
.TP
.BI "const unsigned char *Th8_GetEmbeddedKeyTest(size_t *" pnData ");"
Returns a pointer to the embedded test key data.  If
.I pnData
is non-NULL, the size in bytes is stored there.
.TP
.BI "Th8_RsaKey *Th8_GetPublicKeyTest(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Load the embedded test key as a parsed
.B Th8_RsaKey
structure.  The returned key is cached internally and must NOT be
freed by the caller.  Returns NULL on parse failure.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetPublicKeyTestToken(Th8_Interp *" interp ", char " zOut "[17]);"
Compute the 16-character hexadecimal public key token for the
embedded test key.  The output buffer must be at least 17 bytes.
Returns
.B TH8_OK
on success.
.PP
The test key is preloaded into the policy in debug builds and
when the
.B TH8SH_YES_TESTLIB
environment variable is set.
.SS "Memory: Overflow-Safe Allocation"
.TP
.BI "void *Th8_SafeAlloc(Th8_Interp *" interp ", size_t " nByte ", const char *" zFile ", int " nLine ");"
Allocate
.I nByte
bytes of zero-filled memory.  Panics on allocation failure.
.I zFile
and
.I nLine
are for diagnostic tracing (typically supplied via the
.B TH8_ALLOC
macro).
.TP
.BI "void *Th8_SafeAllocStr(Th8_Interp *" interp ", size_t " nLen ", const char *" zFile ", int " nLine ");"
Allocate
.I nLen+1
bytes (overflow-safe) for a NUL-terminated string.
.TP
.BI "void *Th8_SafeAllocMul(Th8_Interp *" interp ", size_t " a ", size_t " b ", const char *" zFile ", int " nLine ");"
Allocate
.I a*b
bytes.  Returns NULL if the multiplication overflows.
.TP
.BI "void *Th8_SafeAllocAdd(Th8_Interp *" interp ", size_t " a ", size_t " b ", const char *" zFile ", int " nLine ");"
Allocate
.I a+b
bytes.  Returns NULL if the addition overflows.
.TP
.BI "void *Th8_SafeAllocMulAdd(Th8_Interp *" interp ", size_t " a ", size_t " b ", size_t " c ", const char *" zFile ", int " nLine ");"
Allocate
.I a*b+c
bytes.  Returns NULL if either computation overflows.
.TP
.BI "void *Th8_SafeAllocStrAdd(Th8_Interp *" interp ", size_t " k ", size_t " n ", const char *" zFile ", int " nLine ");"
Allocate
.I k+n+1
bytes (overflow-safe at every step).  Used for the "prefix + tail + NUL"
string-buffer pattern.  Backing function for the
.B TH8_ALLOC_STR_ADD
macro.  Returns NULL on overflow at either internal addition.
.TP
.BI "void *Th8_SafeAllocStrMul(Th8_Interp *" interp ", size_t " n ", size_t " sz ", const char *" zFile ", int " nLine ");"
Allocate
.I (n+1)*sz
bytes (overflow-safe at every step).  Used for "wide-string buffer with
NUL slot" patterns.  Backing function for the
.B TH8_ALLOC_STR_MUL
macro.  Returns NULL on overflow at either internal step.
.TP
.BI "void *Th8_SafeAllocMulAdd2(Th8_Interp *" interp ", size_t " a ", size_t " b ", size_t " c ", size_t " d ", size_t " e ", const char *" zFile ", int " nLine ");"
Allocate
.I (a*b)+(c*d)+e
bytes with four sequential overflow checks.  Used for packed-record
allocation patterns.  Backing function for the
.B TH8_ALLOC_MUL_ADD2
macro.  Returns NULL on overflow at any of the four steps.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_SafeMul(Th8_Interp *" interp ", size_t " a ", size_t " b ", size_t *" pOut ");"
Compute
.I a*b
into
.IR *pOut .
Returns
.B TH8_OK
on success or
.B TH8_ERROR
on overflow (leaving
.I *pOut
unchanged).  No allocation.  Public primitive for callers that need
overflow-checked size math independent of allocation.
.I interp
MAY be NULL.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_SafeAdd(Th8_Interp *" interp ", size_t " a ", size_t " b ", size_t *" pOut ");"
Compute
.I a+b
into
.IR *pOut .
Same semantics as
.BR Th8_SafeMul .
.TP
.BI "void *Th8_AttemptMalloc(Th8_Interp *" interp ", size_t " nByte ");"
Allocate without panicking.  Returns NULL on failure.
.TP
.BI "void *Th8_AttemptRealloc(Th8_Interp *" interp ", void *" p ", size_t " nByte ");"
Resize without panicking.  Returns NULL on failure.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_SecureZero(Th8_Interp *" interp ", void *" p ", size_t " n ");"
Securely zero
.I n
bytes at
.IR p .
Uses volatile writes to prevent compiler optimization.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_Memcmp(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const void *" a ", const void *" b ", size_t " n ");"
Compare
.I n
bytes.  Returns 0 if equal, nonzero otherwise.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_Memcpy(Th8_Interp *" interp ", void *" dst ", const void *" src ", size_t " n ");"
Copy
.I n
bytes from
.I src
to
.IR dst .
.TP
.BI "void Th8_Memset(Th8_Interp *" interp ", void *" p ", int " c ", size_t " n ");"
Fill
.I n
bytes at
.I p
with byte
.IR c .
.SS "Result: Extended"
.TP
.BI "void Th8_ClearResult(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Set the interpreter result to the empty string.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_SetResultDouble(Th8_Interp *" interp ", double " rVal ");"
Set the result to a formatted floating-point number.  Uses
the shortest decimal representation that round-trips
exactly to the original IEEE 754 value, honoring
.B ::tcl_precision
when non-zero.  Special values
.RB ( NaN ", " Inf ", " \-Inf )
are emitted as the corresponding case-preserving string.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_SetResultStatic(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ");"
Set the result to a static string.  No copy is made; the pointer
must remain valid for the interpreter's lifetime.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_ErrorMessage(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zPrefix ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ");"
Set the result to
.I zPrefix
followed by
.IR z .
Used for building error messages.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_WrongNumArgs(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zMsg ");"
Set the result to "wrong # args: should be \e"
.IR zMsg \e""
and return
.BR TH8_ERROR .
.TP
.BI "void Th8_ReportTaint(Th8_Interp *" interp ", size_t " n ");"
Report a tainted string length (high bit set) for diagnostics.
.SS "Coroutines"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_CoroCreate(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zName ", size_t " nName ", const char *" zBody ", size_t " nBody ");"
Create a coroutine command
.I zName
whose body is
.IR zBody .
The first invocation begins evaluation; subsequent invocations
resume after the most recent
.BR yield .
.TP
.BI "int Th8_CoroYield(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ");"
Suspend the current coroutine, returning
.I z
to the caller.
.SS "Expansion Operators"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_RegisterExpansion(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zTag ", size_t " nTag ", Th8_ExpansionProc " xProc ", void *" pCtx ");"
Register an expansion operator for the given
.I zTag
in the current namespace.  The built-in
.B {*}
operator is registered automatically.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_UnregisterExpansion(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zTag ", size_t " nTag ");"
Remove the expansion operator for
.IR zTag .
.TP
.BI "int Th8_FindExpansion(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zTag ", size_t " nTag ", Th8_ExpansionProc *" pxProc ", void **" ppCtx ");"
Look up an expansion operator.  Searches the namespace hierarchy.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_ListAppendExpansions(Th8_Interp *" interp ", char **" pzList ", size_t *" pnList ", const char *" zPat ", size_t " nPat ");"
Append expansion operator tag names to a list, with optional glob filtering.
.SS "Debug API"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_SetDebugCallback(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_DebugProc " xDebug ", void *" pCtx ");"
Install a debug callback.  The callback is invoked before each
command dispatch when stepping is active or a breakpoint is hit.
Pass NULL to disable.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_SetBreakpoint(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zScript ", size_t " nScript ", int " nLine ", int *" pId ");"
Set a breakpoint at the given script name and line number.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_ClearBreakpoint(Th8_Interp *" interp ", int " id ");"
Remove a breakpoint by its ID.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_ClearAllBreakpoints(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Remove all breakpoints.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_ListAppendBreakpoints(Th8_Interp *" interp ", char **" pzList ", size_t *" pnList ");"
Append breakpoint descriptions (id, scriptName, lineNumber triples) to a list.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_SetStepMode(Th8_Interp *" interp ", int " mode ");"
Set the debugger step mode:
.BR TH8_STEP_NONE ", " TH8_STEP_INTO ", or " TH8_STEP_OVER .
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetStepMode(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the current step mode.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_EvalAtFrame(Th8_Interp *" interp ", int " nFrame ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ");"
Evaluate a script in the variable context of call frame
.IR nFrame .
Used for debugger watch expressions.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_NREvalInFrame(Th8_Interp *" interp ", int " nFrame ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ");"
NRE variant of
.BR Th8_EvalAtFrame .
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetFrameCount(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the current call frame depth.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetFrameInfo(Th8_Interp *" interp ", int " nFrame ", const char **" pzName ", size_t *" pnName ");"
Get the name of call frame
.IR nFrame .
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetFrameObjv(Th8_Interp *" interp ", int " nFrame ", int *" pArgc ", const char ***" pArgv ", size_t **" pArgl ");"
Get the argument vector of call frame
.IR nFrame .
.SS "Secure Variable Persistence"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_SecureSetMasterKey(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const unsigned char *" pKey ", size_t " nKey ");"
Set the master key (32 bytes, AES-256) for secure variable persistence.
Copies
.I pKey
into the locked key page (slot 1).
.TP
.BI "void Th8_SecureClearMasterKey(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Securely zero the master key in slot 1.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_EnableSecurePersist(Th8_Interp *" interp ", int " bEnable ");"
Enable or disable the secure persistence security gate.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_IsSecurePersistEnabled(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return non-zero if the secure persistence gate is enabled.
.SS "Fault Injection"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_FaultInstall(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_FaultConfig *" pConfig ");"
Install the fault injection wrapper around the platform callbacks.
All allocation calls are intercepted and can be made to fail
after a configured count.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_FaultUninstall(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Remove the fault injection wrapper, restoring the original platform.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_FaultConfigInit(Th8_FaultConfig *" pConfig ");"
Initialize a fault configuration struct to defaults.
.TP
.BI "size_t Th8_FaultCtxSize(void);"
Return the size of the fault injection context struct.
.SS "Platform Providers"
.TP
.BI "const Th8_Platform *Th8_GetPlatform(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the interpreter's platform struct pointer.
.TP
.BI "Th8_Platform *Th8_ClonePlatform(const Th8_Platform *" pSrc ");"
Heap-allocate a copy of
.IR pSrc .
.TP
.BI "void Th8_FreePlatform(Th8_Platform *" p ");"
Free a platform struct allocated by
.BR Th8_ClonePlatform .
.TP
.BI "int Th8_MergePlatformInterp(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const Th8_Platform *" pSrc ");"
Merge
.I pSrc
into the interpreter's platform, filling NULL slots.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_UseDefaultPlatform(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Reset the interpreter's platform to the process-global default.
.TP
.BI "const Th8_Platform *Th8_GetPosixPlatform(void);"
.TP
.BI "const Th8_Platform *Th8_GetLibcPlatform(void);"
.TP
.BI "const Th8_Platform *Th8_GetWin32Platform(void);"
.TP
.BI "const Th8_Platform *Th8_GetMacOSPlatform(void);"
.TP
.BI "const Th8_Platform *Th8_GetMimallocPlatform(void);"
.TP
.BI "const Th8_Platform *Th8_GetCosmopolitanPlatform(void);"
.TP
.BI "const Th8_Platform *Th8_GetCurlPlatform(void);"
.TP
.BI "const Th8_Platform *Th8_GetEnvPlatform(void);"
.TP
.BI "const Th8_Platform *Th8_GetNullIoPlatform(void);"
.TP
.BI "const Th8_Platform *Th8_GetMemPlatform(void);"
Return the static platform struct for each platform layer.
.B Th8_GetMemPlatform
provides only
.BR xNeedMemory :
on allocation failure it clears the IR cache, validates the size,
and retries via the interpreter's
.BR xMalloc .
.SS "Platform Per-Callback Context"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_SetPlatformContext(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_PlatformFunc " xCallback ", void *" pCtx ");"
Override the context pointer for a specific platform callback.
The
.I xCallback
argument is the platform callback function pointer cast to
.B Th8_PlatformFunc
(a generic function pointer type) to avoid ISO C function-pointer
to object-pointer conversion warnings.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetPlatformContext(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_PlatformFunc " xCallback ", void **" ppCtx ");"
Return the per-callback context override through
.IR ppCtx ,
or the platform default if not set.
.SS "Ensemble Support"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_CallSubCommand(Th8_Interp *" interp ", void *" ctx ", int " argc ", const char **" argv ", size_t *" argl ", const Th8_SubCommand *" aSub ");"
Dispatch to a sub-command by matching
.I argv[1]
against the
.I aSub
table.  Reports an error listing valid sub-commands on mismatch.
.SS "Attribute Flags (Harpy)"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_AttrFlagsParse(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ", int " bComplex ", int " bSpace ", Th8_AfMap *" pMap ");"
Parse a Harpy-compatible attribute flag string into a map.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_AttrFlagsHave(const Th8_AfMap *" pMap ", th8_int64_t " key ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ", int " bAll ", int " bStrict ");"
Test whether the parsed map contains the specified flags.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_AttrFlagsChange(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_AfMap *" pMap ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ", th8_int64_t " key ");"
Apply +add, -remove, and =set operators to the flag map.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_AttrFlagsFormat(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const Th8_AfMap *" pMap ", int " bLegacy ", int " bCompact ", int " bSpace ", int " bSort ", char **" pz ", size_t *" pn ");"
Format the flag map back to a string.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_HarpySigLoad(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zSig ", size_t " nSig ", unsigned char **" ppSig ", size_t *" pnSig ", char **" pzToken ");"
Parse a .b64sig Harpy signature file.
.SS "Miscellaneous Accessors"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GlobMatch(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zPat ", size_t " nPat ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ");"
Test whether
.I z
matches the glob pattern
.IR zPat .
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetEvalDepth(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the current script evaluation nesting depth.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetLine(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the current source line number.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetErrorLine(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the line where the most recent error occurred.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_SetErrorLine(Th8_Interp *" interp ", int " nLine ");"
Set the error line number.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetAllocLimit(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the memory allocation limit in bytes.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetResultLimit(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the result size limit in bytes.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetOverflowCheck(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return non-zero if integer overflow checking is enabled.
.TP
.BI "const char *Th8_GetSourceName(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the name of the current source script.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_PushSourceName(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ");"
Push a source name onto the [info script] stack.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_PopSourceName(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Pop the current source name from the stack.
.TP
.BI "th8_int64_t Th8_GetStepCount(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the current step counter value.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_ResetStepCount(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Reset the step counter to zero.
.TP
.BI "th8_int64_t Th8_GetStepLimit(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the step limit.
.TP
.BI "th8_int64_t Th8_GetTimeMs(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the current time in milliseconds since the epoch.
.TP
.BI "th8_int64_t Th8_GetTimeUs(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the current time in microseconds since the epoch.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetPid(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the current process ID.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetParentPid(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the parent process ID.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetThreadId(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the current thread ID.
.TP
.BI "const char *Th8_GetBasePath(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the base directory path.
.TP
.BI "char *Th8_GetEnv(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zName ");"
Return the value of environment variable
.IR zName .
The returned string is owned by the caller and must be freed.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_DoesEnvExist(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zName ");"
Return non-zero if the environment variable exists.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_KeyValue(Th8_Interp *" interp ", int " op ", const char *" zName ", size_t " nName ", const char *" zValue ", size_t " nValue ");"
Dispatch a key-value operation (TH8_KV_*) to the platform's
.B xKeyValue
callback.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_Sleep(Th8_Interp *" interp ", int " ms ");"
Sleep for
.I ms
milliseconds with cancellation checks every 50ms.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_DeclareSystemVar(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ");"
Register a variable name as read-only from scripts.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_IsSystemVar(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ");"
Return non-zero if the variable is declared as a system variable.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_ExistsArrayVar(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ");"
Return non-zero if the variable is an array.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_DeleteCommand(Th8_Interp *" interp ", th8_uint64_t " token ");"
Delete a command by its token.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetCommandInfo(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ", Th8_CommandProc *" pxProc ", void **" ppCtx ");"
Look up a command's callback and context by name.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_EvalTrusted(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ");"
Evaluate a script with the TH8_EVAL_TRUSTED flag,
bypassing signed-only checks.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_EnableBigint(Th8_Interp *" interp ", int " bEnable ");"
Enable or disable arbitrary precision integer support.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_IsBigintEnabled(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return non-zero if bigint support is enabled.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_IntCmpXchg(volatile int *" p ", int " oldVal ", int " newVal ");"
Atomic compare-and-exchange.  Returns non-zero if
.I *p
was
.I oldVal
and was set to
.IR newVal .
.TP
.BI "void Th8_GetCacheStats(Th8_Interp *" interp ", th8_uint64_t *" pnHit ", th8_uint64_t *" pnMiss ", th8_uint64_t *" pnEvict ");"
Return the IR cache hit/miss/evict counters (requires TH8_BENCHMARKING).
.TP
.BI "void Th8_ResetCacheStats(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Reset the cache counters to zero.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_SetPolicyCallback(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_PolicyProc " xPolicy ", void *" pCtx ");"
Install or remove the policy callback.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_GetPolicyCallback(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_PolicyProc *" pxPolicy ", void **" ppCtx ");"
Retrieve the current policy callback and context.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_SaveSystemVar(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ", void **" ppSaved ");"
Save all elements of a system array variable for later restore.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_RestoreSystemVar(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ", void *" pSaved ");"
Restore a system variable from a previous
.BR Th8_SaveSystemVar .
.TP
.BI "void Th8_SetPackageUnknown(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ");"
Set the script invoked when
.B "package require"
cannot find a package.
.TP
.BI "const char *Th8_GetPackageUnknown(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the current package unknown handler script.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_Pledge(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" z ");"
Call the OpenBSD
.BR pledge (2)
system call with the given promise string.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_Unveil(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zPath ", const char *" zPerms ");"
Call the OpenBSD
.BR unveil (2)
system call.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_OutputError(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ");"
Write to the error output channel.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_EmitTrace(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zFmt ", ...);"
Emit a formatted trace message via the platform's xEmitTrace callback.
.SS "I/O Redirection"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_RedirectInput(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zPath ", size_t " nPath ");"
Redirect stdin to a file.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_RedirectOutput(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zPath ", size_t " nPath ");"
Redirect stdout to a file.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_RedirectErrorOutput(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zPath ", size_t " nPath ");"
Redirect stderr to a file.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetInput(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char **" ppPath ");"
Get the current stdin path.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetOutput(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char **" ppPath ");"
Get the current stdout path.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetErrorOutput(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char **" ppPath ");"
Get the current stderr path.
.SS "Math Functions"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_CreateMathFunc(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zName ", int " nArg ", Th8_MathFuncProc " xProc ", void *" pCtx ");"
Register a math function for use in
.BR [expr] .
.TP
.BI "int Th8_DeleteMathFunc(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zName ");"
Remove a registered math function.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_FindMathFunc(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zName ", size_t " nName ", int *" pnArg ", Th8_MathFuncProc *" pxProc ", void **" ppCtx ");"
Look up a math function by name.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_ListAppendMathFunctions(Th8_Interp *" interp ", char **" pzList ", size_t *" pnList ", const char *" zPat ", size_t " nPat ");"
Append math function names to a list with optional glob filtering.
.SS "List Enumeration"
.TP
.BI "void Th8_ListAppendCommands(Th8_Interp *" interp ", char **" pzList ", size_t *" pnList ", const char *" zPat ", size_t " nPat ");"
Append command names, filtered by glob pattern.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_ListAppendCommandsMatching(Th8_Interp *" interp ", char **" pzList ", size_t *" pnList ", Th8_CommandProc " xMatch1 ", Th8_CommandProc " xMatch2 ");"
Append commands whose dispatch function matches one of the given
function pointers.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_ListAppendGlobalVariables(Th8_Interp *" interp ", char **" pzList ", size_t *" pnList ", const char *" zPat ", size_t " nPat ");"
Append global variable names with optional glob filtering.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_ListAppendVariables(Th8_Interp *" interp ", char **" pzList ", size_t *" pnList ", const char *" zPat ", size_t " nPat ");"
Append current-scope variable names.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_ListAppendNsVariables(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zNs ", size_t " nNs ", char **" pzList ", size_t *" pnList ", const char *" zPat ", size_t " nPat ");"
Append namespace-scoped variable names.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_ListAppendNsChildren(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zNs ", size_t " nNs ", char **" pzList ", size_t *" pnList ");"
Append child namespace names.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_ListAppendVarLinks(Th8_Interp *" interp ", char **" pzList ", size_t *" pnList ");"
Append linked variable names (upvar/global) in the current frame.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_ListAppendLoaded(Th8_Interp *" interp ", char **" pzList ", size_t *" pnList ");"
Append names of loaded shared libraries.
.TP
.BI "void Th8_ListAppendArray(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zArr ", size_t " nArr ", char **" pzList ", size_t *" pnList ");"
Append element names of an array variable.
.SS "RSA Key Internals"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_RsaKeyHasPrivate(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_RsaKey *" pKey ");"
Return non-zero if the RSA key contains a private key.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_RsaKeyModulus(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_RsaKey *" pKey ", const unsigned char **" pp ", size_t *" pn ");"
Return a pointer to the RSA modulus bytes.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_RsaKeyPubExp(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_RsaKey *" pKey ", const unsigned char **" pp ", size_t *" pn ");"
Return a pointer to the RSA public exponent bytes.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_RsaKeyPrivExp(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_RsaKey *" pKey ", const unsigned char **" pp ", size_t *" pn ");"
Return a pointer to the RSA private exponent bytes.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_RsaKeyPrime1(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_RsaKey *" pKey ", const unsigned char **" pp ", size_t *" pn ");"
Return a pointer to the first RSA prime factor.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_RsaKeyPrime2(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_RsaKey *" pKey ", const unsigned char **" pp ", size_t *" pn ");"
Return a pointer to the second RSA prime factor.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_RsaSign(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_RsaKey *" pKey ", const unsigned char *" zData ", size_t " nData ", unsigned char **" ppSig ", size_t *" pnSig ");"
Sign data with an RSA private key using PKCS#1 v1.5 + SHA-512.
.SS "Namespace Helpers"
.TP
.BI "Th8_Namespace *Th8_GetCurrentNamespace(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the current namespace.
.TP
.BI "Th8_Namespace *Th8_FindNamespace(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ", int " bCreate ");"
Find or create a namespace by qualified name.
.SS "Policy Key Management"
.TP
.BI "int Th8_PolicyFindKey(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" zToken ", Th8_RsaKey **" ppKey ");"
Look up an RSA public key in the policy cache by hex token.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_PolicyGetKeyTokens(Th8_Interp *" interp ", char **" pzList ", size_t *" pnList ");"
Append all cached key tokens to a list.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_PolicyPreloadKey(Th8_Interp *" interp ", Th8_RsaKey *" pKey ", const char *" zToken ");"
Insert a key into the policy cache.
.SS "Additional Accessors"
.TP
.BI "const char **Th8_GetCompileOptions(void);"
Return a NULL-terminated array of compile-time option strings.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetLastError(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the platform's last OS error code.
.TP
.BI "char *Th8_GetRealPath(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const char *" z ", size_t " n ");"
Return the resolved real path of a file.  Caller must free.
.TP
.BI "Th8_Hash *Th8_GetMathFuncHash(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the internal hash table of registered math functions.
.TP
.BI "Th8_Hash *Th8_GetPackageHash(Th8_Interp *" interp ");"
Return the internal hash table of registered packages.
.TP
.BI "int Th8_GetEmbeddedKeyTime(Th8_Interp *" interp ", const unsigned char **" ppKey ", size_t *" pnKey ", const char **" ppToken ");"
Access the embedded time key.
.SS "Async State and Event Queue"
.TP
.B "void *Th8_CreateAsyncState(Th8_Interp *interp, void *pCtx);"
Allocate an opaque async-state object that an embedder passes to
.B Th8_QueueEvent
to schedule a callback for later delivery.
.TP
.B "int Th8_FinalizeAsyncState(void *pState);"
Free an async-state object previously returned by
.BR Th8_CreateAsyncState .
.TP
.B "int Th8_QueueEvent(void *pState, int (*xCallback)(Th8_Interp *, void *));"
Enqueue an event for later drain by
.B [update]
or
.BR [vwait] .
.TP
.B "int Th8_DrainQueueEvents(Th8_Interp *interp);"
Drain and invoke all pending events across every event state
associated with the interpreter.
.SS "DNS Resolution"
.TP
.B "int Th8_DnsResolve(Th8_Interp *interp, const char *zName, size_t nName, int eType, Th8_DnsResult **ppResult);"
DNSSEC-validating DNS lookup via the platform's
.B xDnsResolve
callback.
.TP
.B "void Th8_DnsResolveFree(Th8_Interp *interp, Th8_DnsResult *pResult);"
Release a
.B Th8_DnsResult
returned by
.BR Th8_DnsResolve .
.SS "Additional Platform Providers"
.TP
.B "const Th8_Platform *Th8_GetAndroidPlatform(void);"
Return a
.B Th8_Platform
with Android-specific overrides layered on the POSIX platform.
.TP
.B "const Th8_Platform *Th8_GetIosPlatform(void);"
Return a
.B Th8_Platform
with iOS-specific overrides layered on the POSIX platform.
.SS "Additional Filesystem and I/O"
.TP
.B "char *Th8_GetCwd(Th8_Interp *interp);"
Return the current working directory via the platform's
.B xGetCwd
callback.  Caller must free.
.TP
.B "int Th8_GetData(Th8_Interp *interp, const char *zName, size_t nName, char **pzOut, size_t *pnOut, int flags);"
Retrieve named data via the platform's
.B xGetData
callback.
.TP
.B "int Th8_Input(Th8_Interp *interp, char **pzOut, size_t *pnOut, int flags);"
Read input via the platform's
.B xInput
callback.
.TP
.B "int Th8_Output(Th8_Interp *interp, const char *z, size_t n, int flags);"
Write
.I z
(n bytes) to the standard output channel via the platform's
.B xOutput
callback.
.SS "Additional Expression, Signing, and Introspection"
.TP
.B "int Th8_GetExprFeatures(Th8_Interp *interp);"
Return the current expression-feature flag set for the interpreter
(bitwise-OR of TH8_EXPR_* flags).
.TP
.B "int Th8_SetExprFeatures(Th8_Interp *interp, int flags);"
Set the expression-feature flag set for the interpreter.  Returns
the previous flag set.
.TP
.B "const Th8_KeyringEntry *Th8_GetEmbeddedKeyring(size_t *pnEntries);"
Return the array of trusted-root keys embedded in this build; the
count is written to
.IR *pnEntries .
.TP
.B "const void *Th8_GetInternalStubs(void);"
Return an opaque pointer to the TH8 internal stubs table used by
the test library.
.TP
.B "int Th8_IterateArraySearches(Th8_Interp *interp, int (*xCallback)(const char *, size_t, const char *, size_t, void *), void *pCtx);"
Diagnostic enumeration of pending
.B [array startsearch]
state, one callback per array/search-id pair.
.SS "Additional Safe-Alloc and Step-Counter Helpers"
.TP
.B "void *Th8_SafeRealloc(Th8_Interp *interp, void *p, size_t nByte, const char *zFile, int nLine);"
Overflow-safe
.B realloc
wrapper that panics on failure.  See
.B Th8_SafeMalloc
for the family contract.
.TP
.B "void *Th8_SafeAttemptRealloc(Th8_Interp *interp, void *p, size_t nByte, const char *zFile, int nLine);"
Overflow-safe
.B realloc
that returns NULL on failure instead of panicking.
.TP
.B "void Th8_SetStepCount(Th8_Interp *interp, th8_int64_t nCount);"
Set the interpreter's step counter to an explicit value without
changing the step limit.
.SS "Thread Lifecycle"
.TP
.B "void Th8_ThreadInit(void);"
One-time per-thread initialization for a thread that intends to
create or drive a TH8 interpreter (initializes thread-local caches
and per-thread math-function state).
.TP
.B "void Th8_ThreadDone(void);"
Per-thread teardown; releases thread-local storage allocated by
.BR Th8_ThreadInit .
